**Root cause confirmed on direct evidence:** All static end-user hosts (pc3, pc1, pc2, laptop1) have `/etc/resolv.conf` containing only `nameserver 10.5.0.4` — the `search jeremysitlab.com` line is absent. Bare hostname queries sent to srv1's BIND server are refused (RCODE=REFUSED) because the server only serves `jeremysitlab.com` with `recursion no`. The design intent (DHCP global `option domain-name`, wildcard zone) requires the search domain to be present; without it the wildcard is unreachable for bare names, making all application-layer name-based access fail.

